      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "Two of the source's definitional elements are not reconstructed. (1) Definition 8(a), Transparency (p.269), also requires the measure's value range to be a subinterval, proper or improper, of the extended reals; the handbook's statement of Transparency (R 172-180) and W 87-90 give only the joint-table dependence and differentiability, never the range clause. (2) Definition 9 (p.270) states that ordinal equivalence holds iff T' = f(T) for some strictly increasing f; R 291-293 states only that ordinal equivalence preserves comparisons and that increasing transforms preserve rankings, and the converse (comparison preservation yields an isotonic f) is neither stated nor proved. The chapter's theorems, lemmas, examples and notes are otherwise reconstructed and proved.",
